! CP2K input template for Pulay-matrix dataset generation.
!
! Rendered per structure by hotspot_al.cp2k_ml_scf.structures. The recognised
! placeholders are PROJECT, COORD, CELL and KIND, each written in double
! braces; any other placeholder is rejected rather than passed through to CP2K.
! (They are named rather than shown here because this comment is itself part of
! the template, and a shown placeholder would be substituted.)
!
! Three settings here are load-bearing for the dataset and should not be
! changed casually:
!
!   METHOD PULAY_MIXING   -- the whole point. Broyden records no Pulay matrix,
!                            so the sample would be rejected for having none.
!   NBUFFER 8             -- the history depth, and therefore the size of B.
!                            A dataset with one depth teaches a model one
!                            input shape.
!   &AO_MATRICES           -- DENSITY and OVERLAP are how the trajectory and
!                            the electron-count check (Tr(P S)) get their data.
!                            Printing is O(nao^2) per iteration, which is why
!                            this template is for dataset runs only.

&GLOBAL
  PROJECT {{PROJECT}}
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY
  PRINT_LEVEL MEDIUM
&END GLOBAL
&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD QUICKSTEP
  &DFT
    BASIS_SET_FILE_NAME BASIS_MOLOPT
    POTENTIAL_FILE_NAME POTENTIAL
    &SCF
      EPS_SCF 1.0E-6
      MAX_SCF 60
      &MIXING
        METHOD PULAY_MIXING
        ALPHA 0.4
        NBUFFER 8
      &END MIXING
    &END SCF
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PBE
      &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
    &END XC
    &MGRID
      CUTOFF 320
      REL_CUTOFF 50
    &END MGRID
    &PRINT
      &AO_MATRICES
        DENSITY .TRUE.
        OVERLAP .TRUE.
        NDIGITS 12
      &END AO_MATRICES
    &END PRINT
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
{{CELL}}
    &END CELL
    &COORD
{{COORD}}
    &END COORD
{{KIND}}
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
